#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:1
msgid "Experimental Local Overlay Store"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:3
#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:161
#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:185
#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:330
msgid "**Warning**"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:5
msgid ""
"This store is part of an [experimental feature](../../development/"
"experimental-features.md)."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:8
msgid ""
"To use this store, make sure the [`local-overlay-store` experimental feature]"
"(../../development/experimental-features.md#xp-feature-local-overlay-store) "
"is enabled. For example, include the following in [`nix.conf`](../../command-"
"ref/conf-file.md):"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:17
msgid "**Store URL format**: `local-overlay`"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:19
msgid ""
"This store type is a variation of the \\[local store\\] designed to leverage "
"Linux's [Overlay Filesystem](https://docs.kernel.org/filesystems/"
"overlayfs.html) (OverlayFS for short). Just as OverlayFS combines a lower "
"and upper filesystem by treating the upper one as a patch against the lower, "
"the local overlay store combines a lower store with an upper almost-\\[local "
"store\\]. (\"almost\" because while the upper filesystems for OverlayFS is "
"valid on its own, the upper almost-store is not a valid local store on its "
"own because some references will dangle.) To use this store, you will first "
"need to configure an OverlayFS mountpoint [appropriately](#example-"
"filesystem-layout) as Nix will not do this for you (though it will verify "
"the mountpoint is configured correctly)."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:24
msgid "Conceptual parts of a local overlay store"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:26
msgid ""
"_This is a more abstract/conceptual description of the parts of a layered "
"store, an authoritative reference. For more \"practical\" instructions, see "
"the worked-out example in the next subsection._"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:29
msgid "The parts of a local overlay store are as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:31
msgid "**Lower store**:"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:33
msgid ""
"Specified with the [`lower-store`](#store-experimental-local-overlay-store-"
"lower-store) setting."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:35
msgid ""
"This is any store implementation that includes a store directory as part of "
"the native operating system filesystem. For example, this could be a \\"
"[local store\\], \\[local daemon store\\], or even another local overlay "
"store."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:38
msgid ""
"The local overlay store never tries to modify the lower store in any way. "
"Something else could modify the lower store, but there are restrictions on "
"this Nix itself requires that this store only grow, and not change in other "
"ways. For example, new store objects can be added, but deleting or modifying "
"store objects is not allowed in general, because that will confuse and "
"corrupt any local overlay store using those objects. (In addition, the "
"underlying filesystem overlay mechanism may impose additional restrictions, "
"see below.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:44
msgid ""
"The lower store must not change while it is mounted as part of an overlay "
"store. To ensure it does not, you might want to mount the store directory "
"read-only (which then requires the \\[read-only\\] parameter to be set to "
"`true`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:47
msgid "**Lower store directory**:"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:49
msgid "Specified with `lower-store.real` setting."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:51
msgid "This is the directory used/exposed by the lower store."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:53
msgid ""
"As specified above, Nix requires the local store can only grow not change in "
"other ways. Linux's OverlayFS in addition imposes the further requirement "
"that this directory cannot change at all. That means that, while any local "
"overlay store exists that is using this store as a lower store, this "
"directory must not change."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:57
msgid "**Lower metadata source**:"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:59
msgid ""
"Not directly specified. A consequence of the `lower-store` setting, "
"depending on the type of lower store chosen."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:62
msgid ""
"This is abstract, just some way to read the metadata of lower store [store "
"objects](../../store/store-object.md). For example it could be a SQLite "
"database (for the \\[local store\\]), or a socket connection (for the \\"
"[local daemon store\\])."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:65
msgid ""
"This need not be writable. As stated above a local overlay store never tries "
"to modify its lower store. The lower store's metadata is considered part of "
"the lower store, just as the store's [file system objects](../../store/file-"
"system-object.md) that appear in the store directory are."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:69
msgid "**Upper almost-store**:"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:71
msgid ""
"Not directly specified. Instead the constituent parts are independently "
"specified as described below."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:74
msgid ""
"This is almost but not quite just a \\[local store\\]. That is because taken "
"in isolation, not as part of a local overlay store, by itself, it would "
"appear corrupted. But combined with everything else as part of an overlay "
"local store, it is valid."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:78
msgid "**Upper layer directory**:"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:80
msgid ""
"Specified with [`upper-layer`](#store-experimental-local-overlay-store-upper-"
"layer) setting."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:82
msgid ""
"This contains additional [store objects](../../store/store-object.md) (or, "
"strictly speaking, their [file system objects](../../store/file-system-"
"object.md) that the local overlay store will extend the lower store with)."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:85
msgid "**Upper store directory**:"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:87
msgid ""
"Specified with the [`real`](#store-experimental-local-overlay-store-real) "
"setting. This the same as the base local store setting, and can also be "
"indirectly specified with the [`root`](#store-experimental-local-overlay-"
"store-root) setting."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:90
msgid "This contains all the store objects from each of the two directories."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:92
msgid ""
"The lower store directory and upper layer directory are combined via "
"OverlayFS to create this directory. Nix doesn't do this itself, because it "
"typically wouldn't have the permissions to do so, so it is the "
"responsibility of the user to set this up first. Nix can, however, "
"optionally check that the OverlayFS mount settings appear as expected, "
"matching Nix's own settings."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:96
msgid "**Upper SQLite database**:"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:98
msgid ""
"Not directly specified. The location of the database instead depends on the "
"[`state`](#store-experimental-local-overlay-store-state) setting. It is "
"always `${state}/db`."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:102
msgid ""
"This contains the metadata of all of the upper layer [store objects](../../"
"store/store-object.md) (everything beyond their file system objects), and "
"also duplicate copies of some lower layer store object's metadata. The "
"duplication is so the metadata for the [closure](../../glossary.md#gloss-"
"closure) of upper layer [store objects](../../store/store-object.md) can be "
"found entirely within the upper layer. (This allows us to use the same SQL "
"Schema as the \\[local store\\]'s SQLite database, as foreign keys in that "
"schema enforce closure metadata to be self-contained in this way.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:109
msgid "Example filesystem layout"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:111
msgid ""
"Here is a worked out example of usage, following the concepts in the "
"previous section."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:113
msgid "Say we have the following paths:"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:115
msgid "`/mnt/example/merged-store/nix/store`"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:117
msgid "`/mnt/example/store-a/nix/store`"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:119
msgid "`/mnt/example/store-b`"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:121
msgid ""
"Then the following store URI can be used to access a local-overlay store at "
"`/mnt/example/merged-store`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:123
msgid ""
"```\n"
"local-overlay://?root=/mnt/example/merged-store&lower-store=/mnt/example/"
"store-a&upper-layer=/mnt/example/store-b\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:127
msgid ""
"The lower store directory is located at `/mnt/example/store-a/nix/store`, "
"while the upper layer is at `/mnt/example/store-b`."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:129
msgid ""
"Before accessing the overlay store you will need to ensure the OverlayFS "
"mount is set up correctly:"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:131
msgid ""
"```shell\n"
"mount -t overlay overlay \\\n"
"  -o lowerdir=\"/mnt/example/store-a/nix/store\" \\\n"
"  -o upperdir=\"/mnt/example/store-b\" \\\n"
"  -o workdir=\"/mnt/example/workdir\" \\\n"
"  \"/mnt/example/merged-store/nix/store\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:139
msgid ""
"Note that OverlayFS requires `/mnt/example/workdir` to be on the same volume "
"as the `upperdir`."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:141
msgid ""
"By default, Nix will check that the mountpoint as been set up correctly and "
"fail with an error if it has not. You can override this behaviour by passing "
"[`check-mount=false`](#store-experimental-local-overlay-store-check-mount) "
"if you need to."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:144
msgid "Settings"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:146
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-experimental-local-overlay-store-build-dir\">[`build-dir`]"
"(#store-experimental-local-overlay-store-build-dir)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:148
msgid ""
"The directory on the host, in which derivations' temporary build directories "
"are created."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:150
msgid ""
"If not set, Nix will use the `builds` subdirectory of its configured state "
"directory."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:152
msgid ""
"Note that builds are often performed by the Nix daemon, so its `build-dir` "
"applies."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:154
msgid ""
"Nix will create this directory automatically with suitable permissions if it "
"does not exist. Otherwise its permissions must allow all users to traverse "
"the directory (i.e. it must have `o+x` set, in unix parlance) for non-"
"sandboxed builds to work correctly."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:157
msgid ""
"This is also the location where [`--keep-failed`](../../command-ref/opt-"
"common.md#opt-keep-failed) leaves its files."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:159
msgid ""
"If Nix runs without sandbox, or if the platform does not support sandboxing "
"with bind mounts (e.g. macOS), then the [`builder`](../../language/"
"derivations.md#attr-builder)'s environment will contain this directory, "
"instead of the virtual location [`sandbox-build-dir`](../../command-ref/conf-"
"file.md#conf-sandbox-build-dir)."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:163
msgid ""
"`build-dir` must not be set to a world-writable directory. Placing temporary "
"build directories in a world-writable place allows other users to access or "
"modify build data that is currently in use. This alone is merely an "
"impurity, but combined with another factor this has allowed malicious "
"derivations to escape the build sandbox."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:167
msgid ""
"See also the global [`build-dir`](../../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-build-"
"dir) setting."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:169
#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:273
#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:285
msgid "**Default:** \\``"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:171
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-experimental-local-overlay-store-check-mount\">[`check-"
"mount`](#store-experimental-local-overlay-store-check-mount)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:173
msgid "Check that the overlay filesystem is correctly mounted."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:175
msgid ""
"Nix does not manage the overlayfs mount point itself, but the correct "
"functioning of the overlay store does depend on this mount point being set "
"up correctly. Rather than just assume this is the case, check that the "
"lowerdir and upperdir options are what we expect them to be. This check is "
"on by default, but can be disabled if needed."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:181
#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:279
msgid "**Default:** `true`"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:183
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-experimental-local-overlay-store-ignore-gc-delete-"
"failure\">[`ignore-gc-delete-failure`](#store-experimental-local-overlay-"
"store-ignore-gc-delete-failure)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:187
#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:332
msgid ""
"This setting is part of an [experimental feature](../../development/"
"experimental-features.md)."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:190
#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:335
msgid ""
"To change this setting, make sure the [`local-overlay-store` experimental "
"feature](../../development/experimental-features.md#xp-feature-local-overlay-"
"store) is enabled. For example, include the following in [`nix.conf`](../../"
"command-ref/conf-file.md):"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:200
msgid ""
"Whether to ignore failures when deleting items with the garbage collector."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:202
msgid ""
"Normally the garbage collector will fail with an error if the nix daemon "
"cannot delete a file, with this setting such errors will only be printed as "
"warnings."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:204
#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:251
#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:320
#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:354
#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:360
msgid "**Default:** `false`"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:206
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-experimental-local-overlay-store-log\">[`log`](#store-"
"experimental-local-overlay-store-log)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:208
msgid "Directory where Nix stores log files."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:210
msgid ""
"Defaults to [`NIX_LOG_DIR`](../../command-ref/env-common.md#env-NIX_LOG_DIR) "
"when [`root`](#store-experimental-local-overlay-store-root) is not set."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:212
msgid "**Default:** `/nix/var/log/nix`"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:214
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-experimental-local-overlay-store-lower-store\">[`lower-"
"store`](#store-experimental-local-overlay-store-lower-store)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:216
msgid ""
"[Store URL](../../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md#store-url-format) "
"for the lower store. The default is `auto` (i.e. use the Nix daemon or `/nix/"
"store` directly)."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:219
msgid ""
"Must be a store with a store dir on the file system. Must be used as "
"OverlayFS lower layer for this store's store dir."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:222
msgid "**Default:** _empty_"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:224
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-experimental-local-overlay-store-path-info-cache-"
"size\">[`path-info-cache-size`](#store-experimental-local-overlay-store-path-"
"info-cache-size)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:226
msgid "Size of the in-memory store path metadata cache."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:228
msgid "**Default:** `65536`"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:230
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-experimental-local-overlay-store-priority\">[`priority`]"
"(#store-experimental-local-overlay-store-priority)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:232
msgid ""
"Priority of this store when used as a [substituter](../../command-ref/conf-"
"file.md#conf-substituters). A lower value means a higher priority."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:235
msgid "**Default:** `0`"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:237
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-experimental-local-overlay-store-read-only\">[`read-only`]"
"(#store-experimental-local-overlay-store-read-only)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:239
msgid ""
"Allow this store to be opened when its [database](../../glossary.md#gloss-"
"nix-database) is on a read-only filesystem."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:241
msgid ""
"Normally Nix attempts to open the store database in read-write mode, even "
"for querying (when write access is not needed), causing it to fail if the "
"database is on a read-only filesystem."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:243
msgid ""
"Enable read-only mode to disable locking and open the SQLite database with "
"the [`immutable` parameter](https://www.sqlite.org/c3ref/open.html) set."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:245
msgid "**Warning** Do not use this unless the filesystem is read-only."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:248
msgid ""
"Using it when the filesystem is writable can cause incorrect query results "
"or corruption errors if the database is changed by another process. While "
"the filesystem the database resides on might appear to be read-only, "
"consider whether another user or system might have write access to it."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:253
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-experimental-local-overlay-store-real\">[`real`](#store-"
"experimental-local-overlay-store-real)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:255
msgid "Physical path of the Nix store."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:257
msgid ""
"Defaults to [`store`](#store-experimental-local-overlay-store-store) when "
"[`root`](#store-experimental-local-overlay-store-root) is not set."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:259
#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:303
msgid "**Default:** `/nix/store`"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:261
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-experimental-local-overlay-store-remount-hook\">[`remount-"
"hook`](#store-experimental-local-overlay-store-remount-hook)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:263
msgid ""
"Script or other executable to run when overlay filesystem needs remounting."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:265
msgid ""
"This is occasionally necessary when deleting a store path that exists in "
"both upper and lower layers. In such a situation, bypassing OverlayFS and "
"deleting the path in the upper layer directly is the only way to perform the "
"deletion without creating a \"whiteout\". However this causes the OverlayFS "
"kernel data structures to get out-of-sync, and can lead to 'stale file "
"handle' errors; remounting solves the problem."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:271
msgid "The store directory is passed as an argument to the invoked executable."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:275
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-experimental-local-overlay-store-require-sigs\">[`require-"
"sigs`](#store-experimental-local-overlay-store-require-sigs)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:277
msgid ""
"Whether store paths copied into this store should have a trusted signature."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:281
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-experimental-local-overlay-store-root\">[`root`](#store-"
"experimental-local-overlay-store-root)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:283
msgid "Directory prefixed to all other paths."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:287
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-experimental-local-overlay-store-state\">[`state`](#store-"
"experimental-local-overlay-store-state)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:289
msgid "Directory where Nix stores state."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:291
msgid ""
"Defaults to [`NIX_STATE_DIR`](../../command-ref/env-common.md#env-"
"NIX_STATE_DIR) when [`root`](#store-experimental-local-overlay-store-root) "
"is not set."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:293
msgid "**Default:** `/dummy`"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:295
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-experimental-local-overlay-store-store\">[`store`](#store-"
"experimental-local-overlay-store-store)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:297
msgid "Logical location of the Nix store, usually `/nix/store`."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:299
msgid ""
"Defaults to [`NIX_STORE_DIR`](../../command-ref/env-common.md#env-"
"NIX_STORE_DIR) if unset."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:301
msgid ""
"Note that you can only copy store paths between stores if they have the same "
"`store` setting."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:305
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-experimental-local-overlay-store-system-features\">[`system-"
"features`](#store-experimental-local-overlay-store-system-features)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:307
msgid ""
"Optional [system features](../../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-system-"
"features) available on the system this store uses to build derivations."
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:309
msgid "Example: `\"kvm\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:311
msgid "**Default:** _machine-specific_"
msgstr ""

#: source/store/types/experimental-local-overlay-store.md:313
msgid ""
"<span id=\"store-experimental-local-overlay-store-trusted\">[`trusted`]"
"(#store-experimental-local-overlay-store-trusted)</span>"
msgstr ""

